---
title: "Applied Music – Strings"
code: "MUS-165"
category: "music"
credits: "1"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Teaches fundamentals of string instruments, harp, or guitar. Studies the standard repertoire. Private lessons are available for either 1 or 2 hours of credit per semester. The length of the lessons will be 1/2 hour for 1 hour creditr. All courses in applied music may be repeated for a total of 8 hours for the major and 4 hours for the minor. 1half-hour lessons per week, 4hours practice (laboratory) required. Laboratory 4 hours per week. Total 4 hours per week.
